@startuml activity_swimlane
title Activity Diagram – Flight Booking Process

|Customer|
start
:Search for available flights\n(origin, destination, date, passengers);

|Flight Booking System|
:Query flight database\nfor matching results;
:Return list of available flights;

|Customer|
:Browse and select a flight;
:Choose seat(s);
:Enter passenger details;
:Proceed to payment;

|Flight Booking System|
:Validate passenger details;
:Reserve selected seat(s) temporarily;
:Forward payment request to gateway;

|Payment Gateway|
:Process payment transaction;
if (Payment successful?) then (yes)
  :Return success + transaction ID;
else (no)
  :Return failure reason;
  |Flight Booking System|
  :Release reserved seat(s);
  |Customer|
  :Display payment error;
  stop
endif

|Flight Booking System|
:Confirm booking;
:Generate e-ticket with unique booking ID;
:Store booking record in database;
:Trigger notification service;

|Customer|
:Receive booking confirmation\n(email/SMS with e-ticket);
:View booking details in account;
stop

@enduml
